---
// ── /privacy-policy (EN) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Single canonical privacy policy covering every data flow: companies (B2B),
// talent (B2C), the Offer Accelerator advisory, role applications, and
// WhatsApp/Meta messaging. This is the URL to register in Meta's WhatsApp
// Business onboarding. English only: the site has no Spanish version.
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../content/links';

const siteUrl = 'https://purrfecthire.com';
const pageUrl = `${siteUrl}/privacy-policy/`;
const contactEmail = CONTACT_EMAIL;

// This section is driven by the same flag that turns measurement on, so the
// policy cannot say one thing while the site does another. Set
// PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_NAME to the tool's name when you set PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_SRC.
const analyticsOn = Boolean(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_SRC);
const analyticsName = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_NAME ?? 'a privacy-focused analytics provider';

const meta = {
  title: 'Privacy Policy | Purrfect Hire',
  description:
    'How Purrfect Hire collects, uses, and protects personal data across our search services, the Offer Accelerator advisory, role applications, and WhatsApp messaging.',
};
---

<LegalLayout
  title={meta.title}
  description={meta.description}
  lang="en"
  pageUrl={pageUrl}
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  lastUpdated="October 17, 2026"
  lastUpdatedLabel="Last updated"
>
  <p class="legal-intro">
    This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Purrfect Hire OÜ</strong> ("Purrfect Hire,"
    "we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, shares, and protects your personal information
    when you visit our website, communicate with us, apply to a role, join the Offer
    Accelerator advisory, or interact with us on social media and messaging platforms,
    including WhatsApp. By using our services you agree to the practices described here.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Purrfect Hire runs senior and executive searches for venture-backed companies, and
    looks for talent in the market where the role sits. We work across the United States,
    Europe and Latin America.
  </p>
  <p>
    We run two separate services, and the distinction matters for your data:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Search</strong>, for companies that are hiring ("Companies") and the
      candidates we consider for those roles ("Talent").</li>
    <li><strong>Private advisory</strong>, including Offer Accelerator, Career Compounding
      and individual strategic sessions for senior professionals. These are paid
      engagements separate from consideration in a client search.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Purrfect Hire OÜ is the data controller responsible for your personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
  <p>We collect information that you provide directly, information collected automatically, and information from third parties.</p>

  <h3>Information you provide</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact details</strong> — name, email address, phone number, and country or city.</li>
    <li><strong>Professional information</strong> — resume/CV, work history, skills, portfolio or profile links (e.g. LinkedIn, GitHub), English level, and current or expected compensation where requested on a role application.</li>
    <li><strong>Application and advisory data</strong> — answers you submit when applying to a role or enrolling in Offer Accelerator, including interview notes and progress.</li>
    <li><strong>Company and hiring details</strong> — for Companies, information about your company, open roles, and hiring requirements.</li>
    <li><strong>Communications</strong> — messages you send us by email, web form, social media, or WhatsApp, and any files you share.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <p>
    This website does not use advertising cookies or cross-site profiling.
    The open roles pages request published vacancy information from our recruiting
    service. When you submit a role application, that service receives the information
    and files you choose to send. The founders booking link opens Cal.com, which
    provides its own privacy information before you submit a booking.
  </p>
  {analyticsOn ? (
    <Fragment>
      <p>
        We measure audience with <strong>{analyticsName}</strong>, configured
        without cookies. It records the page visited, the referring site, and
        the country, browser type and device type derived from your request. It
        does not store your IP address, does not set an identifier on your
        device and cannot follow you to other websites.
      </p>
      <p>
        We also count which of our main buttons are used, so we know whether a
        page works for companies, for talent or for Offer Accelerator. What is
        recorded is the name of the button and which of those three journeys it
        belongs to. Nothing you type, no email address and nothing about an
        advisory engagement is ever sent to measurement.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  ) : (
    <p>
      If we add audience measurement, it will be a tool that counts visits
      without cookies and without identifying you personally, and this section
      will say so before it goes live.
    </p>
  )}
  <p>
    Our hosting provider may keep standard server logs, including IP addresses,
    for security and reliability.
  </p>

  <h3>Information from third parties</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Publicly available professional information, referrals, and data from partners or platforms (such as Meta/WhatsApp, LinkedIn, or hiring partners) used to evaluate fit and facilitate introductions.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To assess Talent against the requirements of a role and to present candidates to Companies.</li>
    <li>To deliver Offer Accelerator, including sessions, preparation and feedback.</li>
    <li>To evaluate applications, conduct assessments, and coordinate interviews and offers.</li>
    <li>To communicate with you about our services, your application, scheduling, and support requests.</li>
    <li>To operate, secure, analyze, and improve our website and services.</li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations and enforce our agreements.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Messaging and WhatsApp</h2>
  <p>
    We use messaging channels, including WhatsApp (a Meta Platforms service), to
    communicate with candidates, advisory clients, and Companies. When you message us,
    we collect your phone number, profile name, and the content of your messages to respond
    to you, coordinate next steps, and provide updates about roles or the advisory.
  </p>
  <p>
    We use these channels only to communicate with people who have contacted us or agreed
    to be contacted. We do not sell your phone number. Your use of WhatsApp is also governed
    by Meta's own terms and privacy policy, which you should review separately.
  </p>

  <h2>5. How we share information</h2>
  <p>We share personal information only as needed to provide our services:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>With Companies</strong> — we share relevant candidate profiles and application materials with companies considering you for a role, with your awareness.</li>
    <li><strong>With service providers</strong> — vendors that help us run our business (e.g. hosting, scheduling, email, analytics, and messaging providers such as Meta), bound by confidentiality obligations.</li>
    <li><strong>For legal reasons</strong> — when required by law, to protect our rights, or to prevent fraud or abuse.</li>
    <li><strong>In a business transfer</strong> — in connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>

  <h2>6. Offer Accelerator: what stays private</h2>
  <p>
    Your participation in Offer Accelerator, your payments and our private advisory notes
    are confidential. We do not disclose them to client companies, and we do not use them
    to change how you are assessed.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can be considered for a real vacancy if you meet its requirements. The
    recommendation rests on the same role requirements and evidence standards that apply to
    everyone else. We share no private rubrics, no interview answers, no confidential client
    information and no private advisory notes in either direction. Being considered in a
    Purrfect search is free, and Offer Accelerator is never required.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Legal bases for processing</h2>
  <p>
    Where applicable (for example, under the GDPR), we process personal data on the basis
    of your consent, the performance of a contract or steps taken at your request, our
    legitimate interests in operating a recruiting service, and compliance with legal
    obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep personal information for as long as needed to provide our services, maintain
    candidate and client relationships, and meet legal or business requirements. When data
    is no longer needed, we delete or anonymize it. You may ask us to delete your
    information at any time (see "Your rights" below).
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, update, or
    delete your personal information; to object to or restrict certain processing; to
    withdraw consent; and to request a copy of your data. To exercise any of these rights,
    contact us at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. We will respond in
    accordance with applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Data security</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect personal information
    against loss, misuse, and unauthorized access. No method of transmission or storage is
    completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>11. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    We operate internationally, and your information may be processed in countries other
    than your own, including the United States and the European Union. Where required, we
    use appropriate safeguards to protect your data when it is transferred across borders.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our services are intended for working professionals and are not directed to individuals
    under 18. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the
    "Last updated" date above. Material changes will be communicated where appropriate.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how we handle your data, contact us at
    <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
